# Trivy ignore file
# Add CVE IDs or secret rule IDs here to suppress specific findings.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2024-12345                     # Suppress a specific CVE
#   generic-api-key:path/to/file.txt   # Suppress a secret finding in a specific file
#
# Note: qualitylayer/ and docs/site/api/ are git-crypt encrypted.
# In CI, the security-scan job decrypts them before scanning.
#
# See: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/

# minimatch ReDoS — transitive dev dependency of @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree.
# Fix (10.2.1) requires major version bump that @typescript-eslint hasn't adopted yet.
CVE-2026-26996

# brace-expansion DoS - transitive build-time dependency of the docs sites,
# pinned three levels down: @docusaurus/core -> serve-handler -> minimatch@3.x
# -> brace-expansion@1.1.16. Fix (5.0.8) is a major bump that minimatch@3 cannot
# take, so it is unreachable until Docusaurus moves off serve-handler. Not
# shipped to users: Docusaurus emits static HTML and this only runs during the
# local `npm run serve` preview.
CVE-2026-14257

# braces DoS on deeply nested patterns - no fixed version yet. Build-time only in
# the docs: @docusaurus/core -> chokidar (the `npm start` file watcher) and
# @docusaurus/utils -> micromatch, which match the docs' own file globs, never
# input from a visitor. Docusaurus emits static HTML; nothing of it ships.
CVE-2026-93687

# http-cache-semantics - no fixed version yet. Reached only through
# @docusaurus/core -> update-notifier -> got -> cacheable-request, the build's
# check for a newer Docusaurus on the npm registry. Not shipped to users.
CVE-2026-93748

# zip4.6.1 via tauri-plugin-updater2.13.1: the dual-header advisory requires
# ZipArchive inspection followed by ZipStreamReader extraction. Our sole ZIP
# consumer calls ZipArchive::extract throughout; no streaming reader is used.
# Recheck on updater/ZIP consumer changes, or at this short review deadline.
# https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-m665-v7pm-7grj
CVE-2026-115905 exp:2026-11-05

# zip4.6.1 via tauri-plugin-updater2.13.1: oversized symlink targets can abort
# extraction. The sole ZIP consumer is the Windows updater; Update::download
# verifies the payload with the fixed publisher key before update_flow retains
# any bytes for install. No user-supplied ZIPs reach this Rust extraction path.
# Recheck on ZIP consumers/updater/signing changes or this short review deadline.
# https://github.com/zip-rs/zip2/security/advisories/GHSA-q7v9-x93c-xqv3
CVE-2026-115909 exp:2026-11-05
